          "min": -2.0176
        },
        "category": {
          "n_tokens": 1,
          "mean": -0.0003,
          "min": -0.0003
        },
        "text": {
          "n_tokens": 37,
          "mean": -0.0086,
          "min": -0.3167
        }
      },
      "ink": {
        "ink_px": 6561,
        "area_px": 265300,
        "density": 0.02473,
        "chars": 179,
        "chars_per_1k_ink": 27.28
      }
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        311,
        687,
        1707,
        1002
      ],
      "category": "Text",
      "text": "Upon various occasions in the past, this office has passed upon the applicability of section 63 to various classes of per diem employees. On July 26, 1921, the then Corporation Counsel was asked:",
      "logprob_stats": {
        "bbox": {
          "n_tokens": 20,
          "mean": -0.3661,
          "min": -1.9701
        },
        "category": {
          "n_tokens": 1,
          "mean": -0.0,
          "min": -0.0
        },
        "text": {
          "n_tokens": 48,
          "mean": -0.0005,
          "min": -0.021
        }
      },
      "ink": {
        "ink_px": 10517,
        "area_px": 441136,
        "density": 0.02384,
        "chars": 195,
        "chars_per_1k_ink": 18.54
      }
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        673,
        1045,
        1613,
        1320
      ],
      "category": "Text",
      "text": "\"(1) Whether per diem employees who were not required to work on Memorial Day last are entitled to pay for that day, merely because of the fact that they are members of private organizations of war veterans who paraded with the militia?\"",
      "logprob_stats": {
        "bbox": {
          "n_tokens": 21,
          "mean": -0.3706,
          "min": -1.9732
        },
        "category": {
          "n_tokens": 1,
          "mean": -0.0161,
          "min": -0.0161
        },
        "text": {
          "n_tokens": 50,
          "mean": -0.0022,
          "min": -0.0917
        }
      },
      "ink": {
        "ink_px": 8447,
        "area_px": 259440,
        "density": 0.03256,
        "chars": 237,
        "chars_per_1k_ink": 28.06
      }
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        311,
        1360,
        1833,
        1501
      ],
      "category": "Text",
      "text": "The Corporation Counsel replied (59 Opinions of Corporation Counsel, pp. 144-145):",
      "logprob_stats": {
        "bbox": {
          "n_tokens": 21,
          "mean": -0.3148,
          "min": -1.7924
        },
        "category": {
          "n_tokens": 1,
          "mean": -0.0001,
          "min": -0.0001
        },
        "text": {
          "n_tokens": 24,
          "mean": -0.0002,
          "min": -0.0013
        }
      },
      "ink": {
        "ink_px": 3741,
        "area_px": 216124,
        "density": 0.01731,
        "chars": 82,
        "chars_per_1k_ink": 21.92
      }
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        673,
        1541,
        1733,
        1945
      ],
      "category": "Text",
      "text": "\"The purpose of this act seems to be to require that the veterans therein designated shall be given a leave of absence or holiday on Memorial Day with pay in any event. The fact that the persons mentioned in your question marked (1) would not have been employed, and would not have received any pay on that day, in my opinion is not controlling, and they will be entitled to pay for such day.\"",
      "logprob_stats": {
        "bbox": {
          "n_tokens": 21,
          "mean": -0.2896,
          "min": -1.8752
        },
        "category": {
          "n_tokens": 1,
          "mean": -0.0,
          "min": -0.0
        },
        "text": {
          "n_tokens": 82,
          "mean": -0.0002,
          "min": -0.0116
        }
      },
      "ink": {
        "ink_px": 9315,
        "area_px": 429300,
        "density": 0.0217,
        "chars": 393,
        "chars_per_1k_ink": 42.19
      }
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        311,
        1985,
        1822,
        2220
      ],
      "category": "Text",
      "text": "Under date of April 9, 1937, the then Corporation Counsel, in an opinion addressed to the Comptroller in regard to the subject, said (84 Opinions Corporation Counsel, pp. 258-259):",
      "logprob_stats": {
        "bbox": {
          "n_tokens": 21,
          "mean": -0.2592,
          "min": -1.6283
        },
        "category": {
          "n_tokens": 1,
          "mean": -0.0,
          "min": -0.0
        },
        "text": {
          "n_tokens": 53,
          "mean": -0.0001,
          "min": -0.0007
        }
      },
      "ink": {
        "ink_px": 7753,
        "area_px": 356596,
        "density": 0.02174,
        "chars": 180,
        "chars_per_1k_ink": 23.22
      }
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        673,
        2257,
        1765,
        2855
      ],
      "category": "Text",
      "text": "\"I desire to point out, however, that where a per diem employee is regularly employed five days a week and Memorial Day or Armistice Day happens to fall on a day when such employee would not ordinarily be required to work, he would not be entitled to leave of absence with pay. To hold otherwise would result in compensating such employee for six days in one week, whereas provision is required to be made for only five. Such is not the intent of the Law. Since Memorial Day, May 30, 1936, fell on a Saturday, this limitation should be borne in mind in passing on the present claims.\"",
      "logprob_stats": {
        "bbox": {
          "n_tokens": 21,
          "mean": -0.2671,
          "min": -1.7341
        },
        "category": {
          "n_tokens": 1,
          "mean": -0.0,
          "min": -0.0
        },
        "text": {
          "n_tokens": 131,
          "mean": -0.0001,
          "min": -0.0022
        }
      },
      "ink": {
        "ink_px": 23299,
        "area_px": 654108,
        "density": 0.03562,
        "chars": 584,
        "chars_per_1k_ink": 25.07
      }
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        311,
        2890,
        1833,
        3136
      ],
      "category": "Text",
      "text": "At the time the two opinions last referred to were issued by the Corporation Counsel, section 63 of the Public Officers Law read substantially as follows:",
      "logprob_stats": {
        "bbox": {
          "n_tokens": 21,
          "mean": -0.2152,
          "min": -1.5606
        },
        "category": {
          "n_tokens": 1,
          "mean": -0.0,
          "min": -0.0
        },
        "text": {
          "n_tokens": 30,
          "mean": -0.0002,
          "min": -0.0019
        }
      },
      "ink": {
        "ink_px": 10039,
        "area_px": 375934,
        "density": 0.0267,
        "chars": 154,
        "chars_per_1k_ink": 15.34
      }
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        699,
        3157,
        1810,
        3693
      ],
      "category": "Text",
      "text": "\"It shall be the duty of the head of every public department and of every court of the State of New York, of every superintendent or foreman on the public works of said state, of the county officers of the several counties of said state, to give leave of absence with pay for twenty-four hours of the thirtieth day of May, or such other day as may, according to law, be observed as Memorial Day, and the eleventh day of November, known as Armistice Day, to every person in the service of the state, the",
